  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Regular forms",
   "texto": [
    "Se parte de la forma de **eles** en pretérito perfeito simple y se cambia la terminación **-ram** por **-sse**: **falaram** → **falasse** (hablara), **comeram** → **comesse** (comiera), **partiram** → **partisse** (partiera).",
    "**eu** and **tu** also: **falasse**, **falasses**; **ele**, **falasse**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Irregular forms",
   "texto": [
    "**ter** → **tivesse** (had), **ser** → **fosse** (out), **estar** → **estivesse** (out), **fazer** → **fizesse** (out), **dizer** → **dissesse** (out), **poder** → **pudesse** (out), **ver** → **visse** (out), **dar** → **desse** (out).",
    "Eye: **ser** and **ir** share the **fosse** form."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Unreal status",
   "texto": [
    "To imagine something that does not happen: **Se eu tivesse tempo, viajaria** (if I had time, I would travel). The condition carries **se + conjuntivo imperfeito** and the result is usually **condicional**. In European Portuguese, the imperfect indication is also common, especially when speaking: **Se tivesse tempo, viajava**. Condition is not used in the **se** sentence."
   ]
